## 7. Backend API and Service Boundaries

Implement Google integration in the backend (Cloudflare Worker or the approved server-side integration layer), not directly in public frontend code.

Suggested service boundaries:

- `GoogleOAuthService`
  - Build authorization URL.
  - Validate callback state.
  - Exchange authorization code.
  - Refresh/revoke tokens.
- `GoogleConnectionService`
  - Store connection metadata.
  - Encrypt/decrypt refresh token through secret-management boundary.
  - Disconnect and reauthorization status.
- `GooglePickerSessionService`
  - Provide safe Picker configuration/token strategy required by the chosen Picker implementation.
- `GoogleDriveService`
  - Verify selected spreadsheet metadata and permissions.
- `GoogleSheetsService`
  - Read/write/batch update spreadsheet data.
  - Initialize tabs and headers.
  - Validate schema.
- `PortfolioStorageService`
  - Link spreadsheet to portfolio.
  - Enforce owner/tenant access.
  - Coordinate data-source changes.
- `PortfolioSyncService`
  - Refresh, save, reconcile, and record sync status.

Suggested API endpoints (names are illustrative; align to existing API conventions):

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/integrations/google/oauth/start` | Create authorization URL/state |
| GET | `/api/integrations/google/oauth/callback` | Receive authorization code and complete OAuth |
| GET | `/api/integrations/google/connection` | Read connection status/account display info |
| DELETE | `/api/integrations/google/connection` | Disconnect/revoke integration |
| POST | `/api/integrations/google/picker/session` | Create safe Picker session/configuration if needed |
| POST | `/api/portfolios/{portfolioId}/storage/spreadsheet` | Link verified spreadsheet |
| POST | `/api/portfolios/{portfolioId}/storage/spreadsheet/create` | Create and initialize spreadsheet |
| GET | `/api/portfolios/{portfolioId}/storage/spreadsheet` | Read linked spreadsheet metadata |
| POST | `/api/portfolios/{portfolioId}/data/refresh` | Refresh data from Sheets |
| POST | `/api/portfolios/{portfolioId}/data/save` | Validate and write changes to Sheets |
| GET | `/api/portfolios/{portfolioId}/data/sync-status` | Read sync status |

Every endpoint must:
- Require a valid IndyShares session.
- Verify the caller owns or has authorized access to the portfolio.
- Resolve the correct Google connection server-side.
- Validate all IDs and payloads.
- Apply rate limits and audit relevant actions.
- Return safe error messages without leaking tokens or private provider details.

