## 9. Security and Privacy Requirements

- OAuth callback must validate state and bind the flow to the initiating IndyShares user/session.
- Use exact redirect URI allowlists.
- Protect against CSRF, authorization-code replay, and account/portfolio mix-ups.
- Keep client secret and refresh tokens server-side.
- Encrypt refresh tokens at rest.
- Do not expose tokens to Page Builder custom HTML/CSS/JS or published portfolio runtime.
- Do not pass access tokens to arbitrary third-party scripts.
- Restrict CORS to approved application origins.
- Use secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookies for session flows where applicable.
- Validate ownership on every portfolio and spreadsheet operation.
- Audit connect, reconnect, select, change, disconnect, initialize, read, and write events without logging secrets or portfolio contents unnecessarily.
- Provide a privacy explanation of what data is accessed and stored.
- Provide a user-facing disconnect action and a documented data-retention/deletion policy.

---

## 10. Error Handling and Recovery

Handle at minimum:

| Scenario | Expected behavior |
|---|---|
| User cancels consent | Return to app with connection still Not connected; no fake success |
| Invalid/missing OAuth state | Reject callback and restart flow safely |
| Authorization code expired/reused | Show retry/reconnect guidance |
| Refresh token revoked/expired | Mark reauthorization required |
| User selects non-Sheets file | Reject with clear message |
| User lacks edit permission | Offer read-only mode only if explicitly supported; otherwise reject linking for write workflow |
| Spreadsheet deleted/trashed | Mark storage unavailable and prompt user to select another |
| Spreadsheet permission removed | Mark needs attention and prompt reauthorization/permission repair |
| Sheets API quota exceeded | Retry with backoff where safe; show temporary issue |
| Network/API failure during write | Do not show success; record operation failure and support safe retry |
| Partial batch write | Record partial result and use idempotent recovery strategy |
| Existing incompatible schema | Offer migration/backup path; never clear silently |
| User disconnects Google | Stop future API calls and clear/revoke token material as defined |

Retries must be idempotent where possible. Do not create duplicate tabs, spreadsheets, or records when a request is retried.

