Replace the current mock/demo data interface with real integration states.

### 11.1 Not connected screen

Display:
- Google Sheets/Drive integration explanation.
- `Connect Google` primary action.
- Privacy/scope explanation.
- No fake tabs or example records presented as live user data.

### 11.2 Connected, no spreadsheet selected

Display:
- Connected Google account email (safe display metadata).
- `Choose Spreadsheet` action.
- `Create New Portfolio Spreadsheet` action.
- Disconnect action.

### 11.3 Spreadsheet selected

Display:
- Real spreadsheet name.
- Verified Google Sheets link.
- Connected Google account.
- Schema/setup status.
- Last read/write/sync times.
- Refresh, Save, Change Spreadsheet, and Disconnect actions as appropriate.
- Real tabs and records returned by Sheets API.
- Empty states when the actual sheet has no records.

### 11.4 Loading and failure states

- Show loading while connecting, selecting, reading, writing, or initializing.
- Disable duplicate submissions during an operation.
- Show specific, actionable errors.
- Preserve unsaved UI edits after recoverable errors.
- Never show a green success indicator before backend confirmation.

### 11.5 Remove mock data

- Remove hardcoded sample rows from production integration views.
- Sample data may exist only in a clearly labeled demo mode or automated test fixtures.
- Demo mode must never display fake connected status or a fake real Google Sheets URL.
- Production UI must distinguish `Demo`, `Not connected`, and `Connected`.

