## 12. Acceptance Criteria

The feature is complete only when:

1. User can click Connect Google and complete real Google OAuth 2.0 consent.
2. OAuth callback is validated and tokens are stored securely server-side.
3. The Google account connection is associated with the correct IndyShares user.
4. User can open Google Picker and select a real Google Spreadsheet.
5. Backend verifies the selected spreadsheet and write permission.
6. User can create a new spreadsheet and initialize required tabs/headers.
7. Selected spreadsheet ID and metadata are linked to the correct portfolio.
8. UI displays the real spreadsheet name and URL.
9. UI reads real rows from Google Sheets API; no mock rows are shown as live data.
10. User can create/update data and verify the write in their actual Google Spreadsheet.
11. User can edit the spreadsheet externally and refresh data in IndyShares.
12. Connection and sync states reflect actual API results.
13. Token revocation and reauthorization are handled.
14. User can disconnect the Google account safely.
15. Two different users cannot read or write each other's spreadsheet through IndyShares.
16. No Google token or client secret is exposed to browser code, public pages, custom code, or logs.
17. Existing Page Builder JSON/media storage in Drive remains compatible with the established storage architecture.
18. Error and retry flows do not silently duplicate or destroy user data.

