## 13. QA Test Plan

### OAuth
- Connect with a valid Google account.
- Cancel consent.
- Deny requested scopes.
- Invalid state and callback replay.
- Refresh token success and failure.
- Revoke access from Google Account settings.
- Reconnect after revocation.
- Disconnect from IndyShares.
- Confirm tokens never appear in browser network responses, local storage, or logs.

### Picker and spreadsheet
- Select a valid spreadsheet.
- Select a non-spreadsheet file.
- Select a spreadsheet with read-only permission.
- Select a spreadsheet with edit permission.
- Cancel Picker.
- Select a large spreadsheet.
- Select a spreadsheet with existing tabs/data.
- Select an incompatible schema.
- Create and initialize a new spreadsheet.
- Verify no duplicate tabs/spreadsheets on retry.

### Data operations
- Read actual records.
- Create, update, and delete a record if supported by product rules.
- Refresh after external Google Sheets edits.
- Test concurrent edits/conflict behavior.
- Test quota/rate limit and transient API failure.
- Test partial write recovery.
- Confirm stable IDs survive row reordering.

### Tenant isolation
- Connect two separate IndyShares users to different Google accounts.
- Verify each user sees only their own connection and linked spreadsheet.
- Attempt cross-user portfolio/spreadsheet ID substitution.
- Verify no token or spreadsheet content leaks through public portfolio pages.

### UI
- Not connected, connecting, connected, no spreadsheet, selected spreadsheet, syncing, synced, error, and reauthorization states.
- Desktop, tablet, and mobile layouts.
- Keyboard/touch operation.
- Empty spreadsheet state and populated spreadsheet state.

